cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this simulator or its research record, please cite it as below."
title: "nfl_simulator: a deserve-to-win meter for NFL games"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "dgrifka"
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dgrifka/nfl_simulator"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Gives one deserve-to-win number per NFL game from the plays each team ran.
  Each team's success rate and yards per play, with a takeaway folded into
  each, go through weights fit on 2016-2023; 40,000 closed-form draws per
  game turn the two teams' uncertainty into a single home share. Built on
  play-by-play data from the nflverse project (https://github.com/nflverse),
  with full credit to its maintainers.
